  "schema_notes": {
    "schema_origin": "Extends the previous custom extraction schema to version 1.1.0 for compound target courses and nested requirement groups.",
    "local_ids": "Institution, course, requirement, and group IDs are local identifiers, not official institution or ASSIST identifiers. Requirement and group IDs are scoped to dataset_id; keep articulation rules scoped to this agreement when combining datasets.",
    "source_pages": "Page numbers are one-based positions in the supplied PDF.",
    "course_units": "Units belong to the institution listing the course. Source and target units are retained separately; articulation does not make their unit values equal.",
    "course_operator": "COURSE refers to one canonical course record.",
    "or_operator": "OR requires at least one complete operand or child group. For concentration requirements, complete all of option A or all of option B.",
    "and_operator": "AND requires every operand, or every referenced requirement and child group. It encodes source-course bundles, target-course bundles, and groups; it does not encode prerequisite order.",
    "cross_listed_codes": "No cross-listed course codes are stated in this agreement.",
    "no_course_articulated": "A null source_requirement with this status means the agreement lists no Chabot equivalent. The target requirement still exists; null does not mean the requirement is waived, already satisfied, or globally impossible to fulfill.",
    "dag_direction": "Connect sending-course expressions to receiving-course expressions through their articulation rule, then to the applicable requirement groups. Follow group_ids upward to the root group. These are fulfillment relationships, not prerequisites.",
    "prerequisites": "Null prerequisite edges mean the PDF does not provide prerequisite data; no prerequisite relationships or course order have been inferred.",
    "scope": "The PDF lists nine lower division core courses and four physics alternatives. Complete the core plus either the two-course physics option A or the two-course physics option B. This is not the full 120-unit degree plan and does not establish pre-admission course requirements.",
    "policy_application": "Apply the in-person lab policy when evaluating lab equivalence. CHEM 111L and CHEM 112L are explicitly listed as laboratory courses.",
    "target_requirement": "Version 1.1.0 adds target_requirement to every articulation record. It is a COURSE expression for a single receiving course or an AND expression for a receiving-course bundle. target_course_id is retained for single targets and is null for bundles; that null does not mean the target is unknown.",
    "nested_groups": "Version 1.1.0 adds group_ids and source_instruction to requirement groups. Evaluate the group operator across all requirement_ids and group_ids. Empty lists are absent inputs, not independently satisfied groups. agreement.root_requirement_group_id identifies the synthesized root.",
    "chemistry_bundles": "Chabot CHEM 1A maps to CSUEB CHEM 111 AND CHEM 111L. Chabot CHEM 1B maps to CSUEB CHEM 112 AND CHEM 112L. Each source course is one completion used to fulfill its full receiving bundle; do not double-count source units.",
    "biology_bundle": "Both Chabot BIOS 21B AND BIOS 21A are required for the listed articulation to CSUEB BIOL 140B.",
    "physics_options": "Option A is CSUEB PHYS 125 AND PHYS 126, mapped from Chabot PHYS 3A AND PHYS 3B. Option B is CSUEB PHYS 135 AND PHYS 136, mapped from Chabot PHYS 7A AND PHYS 7C. The agreement does not list a mixed A/B sequence."
  }
